    ('1d4dd1f5-e841-4c8c-9761-2d4ad3eec155'::uuid, 'card_description', 'A doctor ''restored'' this stone circle in 1925, setting stones in concrete. Whether he used the original stone holes is unclear; a farmer had apparently taken the circle apart for gate-posts.', 'A farmer apparently took Kinniside Stone Circle apart for gate-posts in the 18th century. In 1925 its 11 granite stones were set in concrete, whether in their original holes is unclear.', 'teaser-card-s046-rollback:1d4dd1f5-e841-4c8c-9761-2d4ad3eec155:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s046: card_description ''A farmer apparently took Kinniside Stone Circle apart for gate-posts in the 18th century. In 1925 its 11 granite stones were set in concrete, whether in their original holes is unclear.'' restored on Kinniside Stone Circle', '664d093daec343061679b5ba6e63b33c93d7451e9e26d1036416b34f14352a06|4be255db8cc647ab7d20c10f3dc13ec5b327000e181b5c84766274a3b82ee28a|4be255db8cc647ab7d20c10f3dc13ec5b327000e181b5c84766274a3b82ee28a', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24: writer card_writer:teaser-rewrite1-001", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "A doctor ''restored'' this stone circle in 1925, setting stones in concrete. Whether he used the original stone holes is unclear; a farmer had apparently taken the circle apart for gate-posts."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24: checker card_fact_checker:teaser-check1-001 (check1), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "a doctor ''restored'' the stone circle in 1925 [S5]; he set the stones in concrete [S5]; whether he used the original stone holes is unclear [S6]; a farmer had apparently dismantled the circle before that [S4]; the farmer used the stones for gate-posts [S4]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24: verifier card_web_verifier:teaser-verify-006 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "A doctor ''restored'' this stone circle in 1925 [SUPPORTED: http://www.stone-circles.org.uk/stone/blakeleyraise.htm]; The site is a stone circle [SUPPORTED: https://heritagerecords.nationaltrust.org.uk/HBSMR/MonRecord.aspx?uid=MNA117156]; He set the stones in concrete [SUPPORTED: https://heritagerecords.nationaltrust.org.uk/HBSMR/MonRecord.aspx?uid=MNA117156]; Whether he used the original stone holes is unclear [SUPPORTED: http://www.stone-circles.org.uk/stone/blakeleyraise.htm]; A farmer had apparently taken the circle apart [SUPPORTED: https://heritagerecords.nationaltrust.org.uk/HBSMR/MonRecord.aspx?uid=MNA117156]; The farmer used the stones for gate-posts [SUPPORTED: https://heritagerecords.nationaltrust.org.uk/HBSMR/MonRecord.aspx?uid=MNA117156]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('1db67c2f-5523-4e2c-a953-2824a7cb25ff'::uuid, 'card_description', 'A local man walking across this site found worked wooden poles in 2004. The ancient timber path is one of the oldest known in its country, the second confirmed structure from its moors.', 'In October 2004 a local man walking the moors found worked wooden poles: the Hatfield Neolithic Trackway, one of the oldest known timber trackways in England, dating to around 2900–2500 BC.', 'teaser-card-s046-rollback:1db67c2f-5523-4e2c-a953-2824a7cb25ff:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s046: card_description ''In October 2004 a local man walking the moors found worked wooden poles: the Hatfield Neolithic Trackway, one of the oldest known timber trackways in England, dating to around 2900–2500 BC.'' restored on Hatfield Neolithic Trackway', '22012516d0d1cfb10cc32771cc009b57874f817d7b330240c7ca21a2937a27f7|89d0feb205eab5ecfd9559a256d89341f39de45dfd0b1cd7334238fa7cd5efd2|89d0feb205eab5ecfd9559a256d89341f39de45dfd0b1cd7334238fa7cd5efd2', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24: writer card_writer:teaser-rewrite-v-002", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "A local man walking across this site found worked wooden poles in 2004. The ancient timber path is one of the oldest known in its country, the second confirmed structure from its moors."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24: checker card_fact_checker:teaser-check-v-002 (check-v), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "worked wooden poles were found at the site [S4]; a local man walking across the site found them [S4]; the find was made in 2004 [S1, S4]; it is an ancient timber trackway [S1]; it is one of the oldest known ancient timber trackways in its country [S1]; it is the second confirmed structure from its moors [S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24: verifier card_web_verifier:teaser-verify2-002 (verify2), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "A local man walking across this site found worked wooden poles in 2004 [SUPPORTED: https://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=12837]; The finder was a local man [SUPPORTED: http://archaeology.ws/2005-12-27.htm]; He was walking across the site [SUPPORTED: http://archaeology.ws/2005-12-27.htm]; He found worked wooden poles [SUPPORTED: https://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=12837]; The find was made in 2004 [SUPPORTED: https://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=12837]; The site is an ancient timber path [SUPPORTED: https://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=12837]; The ancient timber path is one of the oldest known in its country [SUPPORTED: https://ioahc.net/neolithic-trackway-we-need-your-help/]; It is the second confirmed structure from its moors [UNVERIFIABLE, no proving quote: None]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('1dea486d-6a81-4b61-ac89-bca807ad78ab'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Enclosures with restricted access stood inside this ceremonial center. It sat on a natural plateau at 1,066 m, a gateway for exchange between regions with ties to highland centers.', 'Pre-Columbian settlement in the Cajamarca highlands near Pomahuaca. Its mid-elevation position in Jaen Province suggests a role in the exchange networks linking coast and sierra communities.', 'teaser-card-s046-rollback:1dea486d-6a81-4b61-ac89-bca807ad78ab:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s046: card_description ''Pre-Columbian settlement in the Cajamarca highlands near Pomahuaca. Its mid-elevation position in Jaen Province suggests a role in the exchange networks linking coast and sierra communities.'' restored on Ingatambo', 'c5ac819ecad59a4479cbbb6fec1b6aba7c818c9938557c8bdf6cea5ca423bd1a|a7793f05faaad3d68527e340abfb081bfb6134c43a6f2a1afadfd243c4588708|a7793f05faaad3d68527e340abfb081bfb6134c43a6f2a1afadfd243c4588708', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24: writer card_writer:teaser-write-003", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Enclosures with restricted access stood inside this ceremonial center. It sat on a natural plateau at 1,066 m, a gateway for exchange between regions with ties to highland centers."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24: checker card_fact_checker:teaser-check-003 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the site had restricted-access enclosures [S2]; the site is a ceremonial center [S1]; it sits on a natural plateau [S1]; the plateau lies at 1,066 m elevation [S1]; it functioned as a gateway for interregional exchange [S3]; it had ties to highland centers [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-wave-a2-2026-10-24: verifier card_web_verifier:teaser-verify-006 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/run